Here is a thorough analysis of the `crates/system-adapter-protocol` crate.

---

## Full Directory Structure

```
crates/system-adapter-protocol/
├── Cargo.toml
└── src/
    ├── lib.rs       (protocol types, JSON-RPC envelopes, re-exports)
    ├── client.rs    (Client, ClientBuilder, ClientError)
    └── server.rs    (Server, Handler trait, ServerError)
```

No `examples/`, `tests/` directories, no `build.rs`, and no sub-modules beyond the three source files.

---

## 1. Dependencies (Cargo.toml)

| Dependency | Use | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `arrow-schema` | `SchemaRef` in `DatasetConfig` | `serde` feature enabled |
| `serde` | Serialization for all protocol types | workspace |
| `serde_json` | JSON-RPC envelope handling | workspace |
| `uuid` | `Uuid` as run identifier | `serde` + `v4` features |
| `tokio` | Async I/O for stdio transport | `process`, `io-util`, `io-std` features |
| `reqwest` | HTTP transport | **optional**, gated by `client` feature |
| `async-trait` | `Handler` trait async methods | **optional**, gated by `server` feature |

**Feature flags:**
- `default = ["client"]` — the HTTP client is on by default
- `client` — enables reqwest and `Client::http()`
- `server` — enables async-trait and the `Handler` + `Server` types

No dev-dependencies are declared (tests use only std/tokio).

---

## 2. Public API Surface

### From `lib.rs` (always public)

**Enums:**

```rust
pub enum EtlType {
    S3,   // serde: "s3"
}

pub enum AdbcDriver {
    Flightsql,   // serde: "flightsql"
    Databricks,  // serde: "databricks"
}
// impl Display for AdbcDriver
```

**Structs (protocol data types):**

```rust
pub struct DatasetConfig {
    pub etl_type: EtlType,
    pub schema: SchemaRef,
    pub params: HashMap<String, serde_json::Value>,
}

// Setup
pub struct SetupRequest {
    pub run_id: Uuid,
    pub datasets: HashMap<String, DatasetConfig>,
}
pub struct SetupResponse { pub ok: bool }

// QueryMethod
pub struct QueryMethodRequest { pub run_id: Uuid }
pub struct QueryMethodResponse {
    pub driver: AdbcDriver,
    pub db_kwargs: HashMap<String, serde_json::Value>,
}

// Teardown
pub struct TeardownRequest { pub run_id: Uuid }
pub struct TeardownResponse { pub ok: bool }

// Metrics
pub struct MetricsRequest { pub run_id: Uuid }
pub struct ResourceMetrics {
    pub cpu_usage_percent: Option<f64>,
    pub memory_usage_bytes: Option<u64>,
    pub disk_read_bytes: Option<u64>,
    pub disk_write_bytes: Option<u64>,
    pub disk_read_iops: Option<u64>,
    pub disk_write_iops: Option<u64>,
}
pub struct IngestionMetrics {
    pub rows_ingested: Option<u64>,
    pub bytes_ingested: Option<u64>,
    pub rows_per_sec: Option<f64>,
    pub active_connections: Option<u64>,
}
pub struct MetricsResponse {
    pub resource: ResourceMetrics,
    pub ingestion: IngestionMetrics,
}
```

**JSON-RPC envelope types:**

```rust
pub struct JsonRpcRequest<T> {
    pub jsonrpc: String,
    pub id: serde_json::Value,
    pub method: String,
    pub params: T,
}
// impl JsonRpcRequest<T> { pub fn new(...) -> Self }

pub struct JsonRpcResponse<T> {
    pub jsonrpc: String,
    pub id: serde_json::Value,
    pub result: Option<T>,           // skip_serializing_if = None
    pub error: Option<JsonRpcError>, // skip_serializing_if = None
}
// impl JsonRpcResponse<T> { pub fn success(...), pub fn error(...) }

pub struct JsonRpcError {
    pub code: i32,
    pub message: String,
    pub data: Option<serde_json::Value>, // skip_serializing_if = None
}
// impl JsonRpcError { pub fn new(...), pub fn with_data(...) }
```

**Constant modules:**

```rust
pub mod error_codes {
    pub const PARSE_ERROR: i32 = -32700;
    pub const INVALID_REQUEST: i32 = -32600;
    pub const METHOD_NOT_FOUND: i32 = -32601;
    pub const INVALID_PARAMS: i32 = -32602;
    pub const INTERNAL_ERROR: i32 = -32603;
}

pub mod methods {
    pub const SETUP: &str = "setup";
    pub const QUERY_METHOD: &str = "query_method";
    pub const TEARDOWN: &str = "teardown";
    pub const METRICS: &str = "metrics";
